# Board 0.26, F69 (the product owner's ruling of 2026-10-15): the giving stops at an even share.
# Story: an editor that needs 1200 points is docked on a laptop's 1440. ⌃⌥→ on a terminal, which goes down to next to nothing. The two do not
# fit side by side unless the terminal is a slit, and not even then. Whoever pressed the key for the right half has asked for the half: a window that
# fits is never made narrower than an even share of its row for one that does not fit anyway.
open Editor 1250x800 min 1200x600
open Terminal 585x400 min 177x64
focus 101
press dock left
focus 102
press dock right
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect count docked 2
# The right half, and the editor flush left at its smallest, under it.
expect at 102 726 37
expect size 102 702x851
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 1200x851
expect in-front 102
# ⌃⌥Z, to the point.
press undo
expect floating 102
expect size 102 585x400
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 1200x851
